# CI and commits

- Start each piece of work on a new branch from current `origin/main`. Do not keep coding on a merged or deleted branch.
- One task, one commit. Do not batch unrelated tasks into a single commit.
- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`. If a wrapper inserts that trailer, rewrite the commit so it is removed before push.
- When a pull request has a failing CI check, fix it before stopping. Do not leave lint, typecheck, test, or build failures for the user.
- Do not claim work is done while GitHub checks on the open PR are still failing.
